 species, due to the ferruginous-red markings, apical bands on T 1 – T 2 only and the longer male clypeus with deeper apical emargination (0.55 × as deep and wide) and longer and sharper lateral teeth. Genetic data support this treatment, with a genetic distance from S. fastidiosissimus of 26.56 – 32.05 % (mean 28.19 %).","","text","",""]]},"T86C2":{"d":[["Distribution. India (new record): Karnataka, Kerala, Tamil Nadu. Elsewhere: Nepal.","","text","",""]]},"TD8YN":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"TJQ62":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"TLRM8":{"d":[["Caribbean","","text","",""]]},"TR64G":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"TTHG":{"d":[["Russia (South Siberia), Kazakhstan","","text","",""]]},"TZW99":{"d":[["Distribution: Only known from Iraq, not listed for the fauna of Iraq (Wiltshire 1957), nor for the adjacent provinces of Iran (Rajaei et al. 2023).","","text","",""]]},"V322J":{"d":[["Brazil (Pernambuco)","","text","",""]]},"V3WFQ":{"d":[["Mauritius; La Réunion","","text","",""]]},"VC7VQ":{"d":[["Florida Keys","8965","mrgid","",""]]},"VC85Q":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"VZ6Q":{"d":[["Turkmenistan; Iran (NE-Iran: Mts.)","","text","",""]]},"W96Q":{"d":[["Afrotropical(Zimbabwe)","","text","",""]]},"X9RT":{"d":[["Nepal","","text","native",""]]},"XHTC":{"d":[["BR","","text","native",""]]},"Y752":{"d":[["New Guinea","","text","native",""]]},"YXQ5":{"d":[["Neotropical(Mexico:Sonora)","","text","",""]]}}